    {
      "number": 1,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 5,
      "stem": "The function $f$ is defined by $f(x)=\\dfrac{x-1}{2-x}$, for $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{2\\}$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "State the range of $f$.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find $f^{-1}(x)$.",
          "marks": 4
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "Range excludes $-1$; $f^{-1}(x)=(2x+1)/(x+1)$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-1\\}$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Let $y=(x-1)/(2-x)$ and rearrange."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$x(1+y)=2y+1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=(2y+1)/(y+1)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$f^{-1}(x)=(2x+1)/(x+1)$, $x\\ne-1$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "All angles in this question are in radians.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "",
          "prompt": "Find the exact value of $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/2}8\\sin x\\cos x\\,\\mathrm dx$.",
          "marks": 6
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$4$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin2x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Integral becomes $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}4\\sin2x\\,\\mathrm dx$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "An antiderivative is $-2\\cos2x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Evaluate at both limits."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$-2\\cos\\pi+2\\cos0=2+2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$4$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "Let $f(x)=ax^3+2ax^2+bx+3a$, where $a,b\\in\\mathbb R$ and $a\\ne0$. Its three zeros are counted with multiplicity.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Write down the sum and the product of the zeros of $f$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "The curve $y=f(x)$ has a stationary point at $(1,3)$. Find $a$ and $b$.",
          "marks": 4
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "Sum $-2$, product $-3$; $a=-3$, $b=21$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Sum $=-2a/a=-2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Product $=-3a/a=-3$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$f\\prime(x)=3ax^2+4ax+b$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$f(1)=3$ gives $6a+b=3$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$f\\prime(1)=0$ gives $7a+b=0$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$a=-3$, $b=21$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 5,
      "stem": "The discrete random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution, where $0\\le p\\le0.7$ and $q\\ge0$.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| $\\mathrm P(X=x)$ | $p$ | $0.7-p$ | $q$ |",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find $q$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Given that $\\mathrm E(X)=2.1$, find $p$.",
          "marks": 3
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$q=0.3$, $p=0.2$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "The probabilities sum to $1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$p+0.7-p+q=1$, so $q=0.3$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$p+2(0.7-p)+3q=2.1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$p+1.4-2p+0.9=2.1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$p=0.2$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
